 "note": "What the ground looks like from a metre away. The aerial carries the colour of every square metre; these tiles carry the grain the aerial cannot. Each is a CC0 material from ambientCG, recoloured so its mean matches a sunlit patch in one of the owner's photographs, so the straw is this straw's colour and the drive is this drive's. The world chooses the tile from the aerial's own colour under your feet: straw where it is bright and gold, gravel where it is pale and grey, leaf litter where the aerial shows canopy, dirt otherwise. Building massings use `surfaces` below — scripts call glb.surface(key) and never hardcode RGB.",
